Because they developed a system  of mining, whereby  once once it was  the the the task had begun to clear the coal face  of a certain er a certain area of coal,it didn't matter what what happened during that particular period of time, whether all the machinery broke down, etcetera, etcetera,you had to stop u until that amount of coal had been cleared off, you see.
And they were not having anybody in the mine, with a watch, who could let people know exactly what the time was, and in other words, create a situation where the men might go home before they'd completed this particular task.
